From b0998b20240317511853216274225079fc1b4e7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] net: thunderbolt: Enable E2E flow control on the Tx ring
 if required

When full end-to-end flow control is negotiated, thunderbolt-net enables
it on the Rx ring only. On host interfaces that only honour the credits
on Tx rings that have E2E flow control enabled as well (tb_nhi::tx_e2e,
the Apple NHI), the sender then ignores the credits and overruns the
receiver's ring once that falls behind.

Enable E2E on the Tx ring too when the host interface requires it.

Same-host loopback between two USB4 ports of a Mac Studio (M1 Max,
20 Gb/s x2, MTU 65522, iperf3, 15 s per run; frames dropped by the
receiving ring in brackets):

                    before                   after
  single stream     4.2 Gb/s (5128)          4.8 Gb/s (0)
  4 streams         4.5 Gb/s (18216)         5.0 Gb/s (0)
  bidirectional     2.4 + 2.3 Gb/s (5252)    2.3 + 2.3 Gb/s (0)

TCP retransmits drop from 1600-5600 to 200-700 per run.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/thunderbolt/main.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/thunderbolt/main.c b/drivers/net/thunderbolt/main.c
index 82cef2009..071aff21b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/thunderbolt/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/thunderbolt/main.c
@@ -943,12 +943,19 @@ static int tbnet_open(struct net_device *dev)
 	u16 sof_mask, eof_mask;
 	struct tb_ring *ring;
 	unsigned int flags;
+	bool full_e2e;
 	int hopid;
 
 	netif_carrier_off(dev);
 
-	ring = tb_ring_alloc_tx(xd->tb->nhi, -1, TBNET_RING_SIZE,
-				RING_FLAG_FRAME);
+	/* Only enable full E2E if the other end supports it too */
+	full_e2e = tbnet_e2e && net->svc->prtcstns & TBNET_E2E;
+
+	flags = RING_FLAG_FRAME;
+	if (full_e2e && xd->tb->nhi->tx_e2e)
+		flags |= RING_FLAG_E2E;
+
+	ring = tb_ring_alloc_tx(xd->tb->nhi, -1, TBNET_RING_SIZE, flags);
 	if (!ring) {
 		netdev_err(dev, "failed to allocate Tx ring\n");
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -968,8 +975,7 @@ static int tbnet_open(struct net_device *dev)
 	eof_mask = BIT(TBIP_PDF_FRAME_END);
 
 	flags = RING_FLAG_FRAME;
-	/* Only enable full E2E if the other end supports it too */
-	if (tbnet_e2e && net->svc->prtcstns & TBNET_E2E)
+	if (full_e2e)
 		flags |= RING_FLAG_E2E;
 
 	ring = tb_ring_alloc_rx(xd->tb->nhi, -1, TBNET_RING_SIZE, flags,
-- 
